WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
Prepared QA example: a small documentation change.
The learner supplies a goal and boundaries.

00:02.000 --> 00:05.200
Paused to read the actual AI reply.
The proposed file is ready for review, not yet applied.

00:05.200 --> 00:06.800
“Looks good. I agree with the change.”
The mentor reviews this vague explanation.

00:06.800 --> 00:07.960
The explanation does not establish what the change does.
Apply stays locked.

00:07.960 --> 00:13.200
Paused to read the actual rejection.
The learner is asked to explain what the changed lines establish.

00:13.200 --> 00:15.000
The learner explains the actual effect, preserved boundaries
and limits of the available evidence.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.200
Paused to read the accepted understanding assessment.
The unchanged proposal is ready for explicit Apply.

00:21.200 --> 00:22.560
The learner selects “Apply this reviewed proposal.”
The documentation is saved.

00:22.560 --> 00:30.000
Paused to read the actual saved result.
Execution and phase review remain separate steps.
